112:
The purpose of this code of ethics is to:
(1) Encourage high ethical standards in official conduct by city officials;
(2) Establish guidelines for ethical standards of conduct for all such officials by setting forth those acts or actions that are incompatible with the interest of the city;
(3) Require disclosure by such officials of private financial or other interest in matters affecting the city; and
(4) Serve as a basis for disciplining those who refuse to abide by its terms.
(Ord. of 2-17-2011, § 1)

146:
No holder of a license which authorizes the sale of malt beverages and wine at retail in the city by the package or by the drink, nor any agents or employees of the licensee, shall do any of the following upon licensed premises:
(1) Sell alcoholic beverages to any person while this person is in an intoxicated condition;
(2) Permit on the licensed premises any disorderly conduct or breach of the peace;
(3) Sell, offer for sale, or possess on the licensed premises any kind of alcoholic liquor, the sale of or possession of which is not authorized under this chapter;
(4) Sell malt beverages or wine by the package, either retail or wholesale, within 100 yards of any church, school building, school grounds, or college campus;
(5) Sell alcoholic beverages by the drink for consumption on the premises within 25 yards of any church, school building, school grounds, or college campus;
(6) Sell alcoholic beverages to persons under the legal drinking age as provided by the laws of the state.
(Ord. of 12-16-2021(1))

178:
